            $integral.cont bold(g) dot d bold(A) = -4pi G M_"encl"$ \
            $V_g = -G M\/r$ \
            $U_g = m V_g$
        ],
        [
            #set text(size: 8.5pt)
            source: charge $Q$ (attract / repel) \
            $bold(E) = bold(F)\/q$ \
            $E = k Q\/r^2$ \
            $integral.cont bold(E) dot d bold(A) = Q_"encl"\/epsilon_0$ \
            $V_e = k Q\/r$ \
            $U_e = q V_e$
        ],
    )
    #v(4pt)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: 0.3pt + c-border)
]

== Electric Force & Field

#entry($bold(F) = k frac(q_1 q_2, r^2) hat(r) = q bold(E) quad bold(E) = k frac(Q, r^2) hat(r) = frac(Delta V, Delta d) = integral frac(k thin d q, r^2) hat(r)$, note: [
    $k = 8.99 times 10^9$ N·m²/C². Like charges repel; opposite attract.
])

== Gauss's Law

#entry($Phi_E = integral.cont bold(E) dot d bold(A) = frac(Q_"encl", epsilon_0)$, note: [
    $epsilon_0 = 8.854 times 10^(-12)$ F/m. \
    Inf. line: $E = lambda\/(2pi epsilon_0 r)$; infinite sheet: $E = sigma\/(2 epsilon_0)$.
])

== Potential & Energy

#entry($U_E = q V quad V = k integral frac(d q, r) quad bold(E) = -nabla V$, note: [
    Equipotentials ⊥ field lines. $Delta V = -integral bold(E) dot d bold(r)$.
])

== Capacitors

#entry($C = frac(Q, V) = epsilon_0 frac(A, d) quad U_C = frac(1,2)C V^2 = frac(Q^2, 2C)$, note: [
    Series: $1\/C_"eq" = sum 1\/C_i$. Parallel: $C_"eq" = sum C_i$. \
    Energy density: $u_E = frac(1,2) epsilon_0 E^2$.
])

== Magnetic Force

#entry($bold(F) = q(bold(E) + bold(v) times bold(B))$, note: [
    $bold(F)_B perp bold(v)$; does no work. $|F_B| = |q|v B sin theta$. \
    Current-carrying wire: $bold(F) = I bold(L) times bold(B)$.
])

#entry($Phi_B = B A cos theta quad integral.cont bold(B) dot d bold(A) = 0$, note: [
    No magnetic monopoles; $bold(B)$ field lines form closed loops.
])

== Biot-Savart & Ampere–Maxwell

#entry($d bold(B) = frac(mu_0, 4pi) frac(I thin d bold(l) times hat(r), r^2)$, note: [
    $mu_0 = 4pi times 10^(-7)$ H/m. \
    Infinite wire: $B = mu_0 I\/(2pi r)$. Loop center: $B = mu_0 I\/(2R)$.
])

#entry($integral.cont bold(B) dot d bold(s) = mu_0 I_"encl" + mu_0 epsilon_0 frac(d Phi_E, d t)$, note: [
    Displacement current → EM waves: $c = 1\/sqrt(mu_0 epsilon_0) approx 3.00 times 10^8$ m/s. \
    Ampère's law: static case ($d Phi_E\/d t = 0$).
])


